e` applied to unary input `replicate ℓ true` with `Finite (Γ k)`, which is standard; the quantum gate semantics are written by hand.","note":"`exact_quantum_factoring : MainTheorem := ∃ family : ℕ → Circuit, Uniform family ∧ PolynomialResources family ∧ ∀ ℓ N, 2 ≤ N → N.size = ℓ → ℓ + (paddedLength ℓ)^2 ≤ (family ℓ).qubits ∧ (family ℓ).correctProbability ℓ N = 1` over a fixed 20-gate set (NOT/CNOT/Toffoli/Hadamard/phase with optional inverse and one control), where `correctProbability` is the exact Born probability of outputting the sorted prime factorization with multiplicities (`CorrectEncoding`) and `Uniform` uses a Mathlib `TM2ComputableInPolyTime` generator with finite alphabets. Matches the summary (exact, polynomial gates and qubits, fixed finite gate set).","text":"The challenge statements imply the headline claim after unpacking definitions or one routine step.","url":"https://github.com/mathvet/mathvet/blob/14c7f918cd336d0da03a02aae5a0eed4a429d4db/reviews/openai-math/fidelity-table.csv","verdict":"full"},"source_verdict":"full","state":"all","target":"f:279","target_kind":"family-headline"}],"release_id":"openai-math","remaining_checks":[{"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:4020f1ce26efb73b41103ac37a023c710913a0d7ac2825bcbd4fbaa08e0e9d98","grain":"challenge","id":"challenge:ExactQuantumFactoring","title":"ExactQuantumFactoring"},"kind":"scope-review","reason":"An AI scope draft has no named human review.","target":"l:ExactQuantumFactoring"},{"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:7cfd8e4680208cffee23a1a91f40545c095d7de94ac5e9718bd08934b92419e5","grain":"family","id":"family:279","title":"Exact quantum factoring over a fixed finite gate set"},"kind":"claim-identification","reason":"Lexical navigation candidate; catalogue headline identity requires review.","target":"f:279"},{"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:7cfd8e4680208cffee23a1a91f40545c095d7de94ac5e9718bd08934b92419e5","grain":"family","id":"family:279","title":"Exact quantum f